<Base title="About Clipping Guide & Our Editorial Standards" description="How Clipping Guide researches tutorials, cites sources, explains product comparisons, handles corrections, and keeps earning claims realistic."><div class="wrap page-intro"><h1>A useful place to learn clipping.</h1><p>Clipping Guide is an independent publication about turning longer videos into clear, watchable clips.</p></div><div class="wrap plain-page prose"><h2>Who this is for</h2><p>First-time editors, stream and podcast clippers, creators repurposing their own footage, and people trying to understand paid clipping campaigns. We cover the craft and the practical decisions around it.</p><h2>How we make our guides</h2><p>We use AI assistance to organize research and draft explanations. Guides link to official platform documentation for current product features and rules. Community conversations help us identify questions, but are not treated as proof of legal rights or platform policy.</p><p>Our launch guides are research-based. We do not claim firsthand product testing, professional credentials, creator endorsements, or earnings results that we have not established. A tool comparison explains documented features and tradeoffs; it is not a lab-tested ranking.</p><h2>What you can expect</h2><ul><li>A direct answer before a long explanation.</li><li>Practical steps and examples that are clearly labeled.</li><li>Sources, publication dates, and meaningful update dates.</li><li>Distinctions between campaign payouts, client fees, and platform monetization.</li><li>Clear permissions and context checks before publishing someone else's footage.</li></ul><h2>Independence & commercial relationships</h2><p>We are not affiliated with Whop, YouTube, CapCut, or the other products discussed. At launch, links are ordinary source links, not affiliate links. If a future article contains a paid placement or affiliate link, it must disclose that relationship on the article.</p><h2 id="corrections">Corrections</h2><p>Spot an error or an outdated instruction? <a href="https://github.com/vishprometa/clippingguide/issues/new?title=Clipping%20Guide%20correction">Open a correction request</a> with the page URL, the statement in question, and an official source if available. Please leave private account information out of the request.</p><p>We update the visible date when a guide changes substantively. Source checking dates describe when linked documentation was reviewed, not an assurance that a platform rule can never change.</p><h2>Original visual work</h2><p>The site's editorial artwork is AI-generated for Clipping Guide. It illustrates editing concepts and creator environments; it does not document product tests, real studios, or real people.</p></div></Base>

